import forgelib as F
G = F.make(slug="the-forge-combat-guide", order=23, kw="block and parry in the forge",
 title="How to Block and Parry in The Forge (+ Boss Tips)",
 h1="How to Block and Parry in The Forge, and How to Beat the Bosses",
 desc="How to block and parry in The Forge on PC and mobile, when to dodge instead, the full controls, and how to fight the Golem and other bosses. Take less damage!",
 kw2=["the forge how to parry","the forge how to block","the forge controls","the forge bosses","the forge golem boss"],
 related=["the-forge-island-3-guide","the-forge-volcanic-depths","the-forge-armor-guide","the-forge-races-guide"],
 ids=["l0RBaPDTXfc","sHHgEuaZ5GA"],
 lead="Most deaths in The Forge come from taking hits you could have stopped. Fridge's Shorts show how to <strong>block and parry in The Forge</strong> and how to handle bosses. Here are the controls and timing tips, checked against two combat guides and the Forge Wiki.",
 heading="Watch Fridge's Combat Shorts",
 sections=[
 ("block","How to Block","""<ol class="steps"><li>Equip a <strong>weapon</strong>, not your pickaxe. Blocking and parrying only work with a weapon out.</li><li>On PC, <strong>hold F</strong> as an enemy attacks. On mobile, press the <strong>shield</strong> button.</li><li>Your character takes a blocking stance and takes less damage.</li></ol>
<p>The Spike's controls table notes that block needs <strong>Shift-Lock</strong> (Ctrl) turned on, and that holding block too long drains Stamina.</p>"""),
 ("parry","How to Parry","""<p>A parry is a perfectly timed block. Press <strong>F</strong> (or the shield) at the <strong>exact moment</strong> the enemy's attack connects. If you time it right, the hit does no damage and the enemy is briefly stunned, which gives you a free counterattack. Both esports.gg and The Spike describe the same timing.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Practice on heavy hitters.</strong> Esports.gg recommends slow, heavy-weapon enemies like the Elite Zombie, Deathaxe Skeleton, Elite Deathaxe Skeleton and Reaper, because their wind-ups are easy to read.</li><li><strong>Watch for red particles.</strong> Slimes and Blazing Slimes glow red just before they attack, which is your parry cue.</li><li><strong>Felynx</strong> players get a passive 20% chance to parry the next attack.</li></ul>"""),
 ("controls","The Forge Combat Controls (PC)","""<div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Controls (The Spike)</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Action</th><th scope="col">Key</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Light attack</td><td>Left mouse button</td></tr><tr><td>Heavy attack</td><td>R or right mouse button (Shift-Lock)</td></tr><tr><td>Block / parry</td><td>F (Shift-Lock)</td></tr><tr><td>Dash</td><td>Q</td></tr><tr><td>Sprint</td><td>Shift</td></tr><tr><td>Shift-Lock</td><td>Ctrl</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Once you can block and parry in The Forge reliably, dash through the attacks you can't block. Fast enemies and big slams are usually better dodged than parried.</p>"""),
 ("bosses","How to Fight Bosses","""<p>The <strong>Golem</strong> was the first boss added. It's an Ice Titan at The Peak on Island 3, reached through the <strong>Colossal Gate</strong>, which opens from XX:00 to XX:15 and XX:30 to XX:45. Its 25,000 HP scales with party size, and it has four attacks, according to the Forge Wiki. Other boss-style fights include the Yeti at The Peak, the Prismarine Spider in the Frost Nest, and the Demonic Queen Spider for Raven 3.</p>
<ul><li>Learn one attack pattern at a time and parry only the moves you can read.</li><li>Bring Health Potions. Health Potion III restores 500 HP over 5 seconds.</li><li>Tanky races help. Golem gives +30% Health, and Dragonborn gives +20% Health and +12% damage. See our <a href="the-forge-races-guide.html">races guide</a>.</li><li>Upgrade your armor first with our <a href="the-forge-armor-guide.html">armor guide</a>.</li></ul>""")],
 faq=[("How do you parry in The Forge?","With a weapon equipped, press F on PC, or the shield button on mobile, right as the enemy's attack lands."),
      ("Why can't I block in The Forge?","You're probably holding your pickaxe. Equip a weapon, and on PC turn on Shift-Lock."),
      ("When does the Golem boss spawn?","The Colossal Gate at The Peak opens from XX:00 to XX:15 and from XX:30 to XX:45 each hour.")],
 sources=[("The Spike: How to block and parry in The Forge","https://www.thespike.gg/roblox/the-forge/how-to-block-and-parry"),("esports.gg: How to parry in The Forge","https://esports.gg/guides/roblox/how-to-parry-in-the-forge/"),F.wiki("Golem","Golem boss"),F.wiki("Races"),F.wiki("Items","Items (Health Potions)")],
 howto=("How to parry in The Forge",[("Equip a weapon","Switch from your pickaxe to a weapon.","block"),("Turn on Shift-Lock","On PC, press Ctrl.","block"),("Time it","Press F right as the attack connects.","parry"),("Counter","Hit the stunned enemy.","parry")]))
